WEBVTT

00:04.650 --> 00:07.250
Welcome to Boonesboro Quarry. It's an underground

00:07.250 --> 00:09.763
limestone mine that The Allen Company has owned

00:09.763 --> 00:13.388
and operated since 1939. It sits along the Kentucky

00:13.388 --> 00:16.125
River in northern Madison County, off Kentucky

00:16.125 --> 00:23.125
Highway 627. Its MSHA mine ID is 15-00006,

00:23.125 --> 00:26.000
one of the oldest active limestone mine IDs in

00:26.000 --> 00:28.925
the state. This drawing is an illustration to help

00:28.925 --> 00:31.438
you picture the site. It isn't a map.

00:31.438 --> 00:33.500
Your instructor will show you the real one.

00:34.633 --> 00:37.070
The mine works the Camp Nelson Limestone,

00:37.070 --> 00:39.833
the same rock unit mined at Dix River Stone,

00:39.833 --> 00:43.383
using room and pillar. Rooms here are about 35

00:43.383 --> 00:46.733
by 45 feet. Allen's own crew does the drilling

00:46.733 --> 00:49.733
and blasting, and site leadership includes licensed

00:49.733 --> 00:52.795
blasters. The property sits near the Kentucky River

00:52.795 --> 00:55.883
Fault System, so ground conditions and geologic

00:55.883 --> 00:58.795
structure are an everyday part of mining safely

00:58.795 --> 00:59.545
here.

01:00.678 --> 01:03.703
Boonesboro has three levels. Active mining is on

01:03.703 --> 01:06.978
Level 2 and Level 3. The primary crusher is on

01:06.978 --> 01:10.103
Level 2, and crushed rock is conveyed outside to

01:10.103 --> 01:13.103
the surface screens and secondary crushers.

01:13.103 --> 01:15.428
Because of the levels, the first thing to know

01:15.428 --> 01:18.453
every shift is which level you're working on today.

01:18.453 --> 01:21.566
It decides your escapeways, your travel route and

01:21.566 --> 01:22.753
where you'll be counted.

01:23.880 --> 01:27.030
Rock is stockpiled on the surface and on Level 1,

01:27.030 --> 01:29.892
where the mine shop is. Boonesboro also runs a

01:29.892 --> 01:32.918
Liwell screen plant, a dry screen plant that produces

01:32.918 --> 01:36.118
a very clean product used in asphalt mix.

01:36.118 --> 01:38.680
And product is hauled to the stockpile at the blacktop

01:38.680 --> 01:42.293
plant known as BT3, Boonesboro Blacktop.

01:42.293 --> 01:46.918
To reach BT3 you travel under the KY 627 bridge.

01:48.055 --> 01:50.230
The products are crushed stone base,

01:50.230 --> 01:57.305
DGA, number 67s, 57s, 9s, 11s, 3s, 4s and 5s,

01:57.305 --> 02:00.505
and CCI. They support construction aggregate,

02:00.505 --> 02:03.642
ag lime and Allen's asphalt operations in Central

02:03.642 --> 02:04.542
Kentucky.

02:05.676 --> 02:08.364
Ground control is the first hazard on Boonesboro's

02:08.364 --> 02:11.701
list. Work only under ground that has been examined

02:11.701 --> 02:14.339
and supported under the ground control plan.

02:14.339 --> 02:17.964
Report cracking, spalling, water or unusual sounds

02:17.964 --> 02:20.476
right away. And scale only if you've been trained

02:20.476 --> 02:23.126
and authorized. Rock that looks solid from the

02:23.126 --> 02:26.101
floor can be loose, and the face is where our one

02:26.101 --> 02:27.951
falling-rock injury happened.

02:29.083 --> 02:31.270
Here's the full list of focus hazards for this

02:31.270 --> 02:34.732
site. Roof and rib conditions. Mobile equipment

02:34.732 --> 02:37.170
traffic underground and on the surface,

02:37.170 --> 02:40.157
loaders and haul trucks. The conveyor system from

02:40.157 --> 02:43.482
Level 2 to the surface. Activity at the shop on

02:43.482 --> 02:47.208
Level 1. The Liwell plant. The haul route to BT3

02:47.208 --> 02:52.320
under KY 627. Silica dust, noise and diesel equipment.

02:52.320 --> 02:55.170
And emergency escape from more than one level.

02:55.170 --> 02:57.320
Every one of them has its own training in this

02:57.320 --> 02:59.895
course, and every one of them is part of a normal

02:59.895 --> 03:00.858
day here.

03:04.180 --> 03:06.730
The site supervisor is Dustin Conn,

03:06.730 --> 03:09.018
and the mine foreman is Kendell Barnes,

03:09.018 --> 03:12.280
both with long underground and equipment experience.

03:12.280 --> 03:15.755
Above them, Hunter Kenney is over all of our sites.

03:15.755 --> 03:17.743
Your instructor will introduce them,

03:17.743 --> 03:20.568
and you report to them or the designated lead before

03:20.568 --> 03:23.530
starting work. Miners check in and out on the tag

03:23.530 --> 03:26.205
board. Visitors and contractors have their own

03:26.205 --> 03:29.105
separate check-in. Never tag in for someone else,

03:29.105 --> 03:31.818
and always tag out when you leave underground.

03:32.951 --> 03:35.775
The traffic rules are simple and they don't change.

03:35.775 --> 03:38.750
The speed limit is 15 miles an hour on the surface

03:38.750 --> 03:41.500
and 25 underground. Haul trucks have the right

03:41.500 --> 03:45.050
of way. All roads are two-way, right-hand traffic.

03:45.050 --> 03:47.388
Before you approach a haul truck, make a radio

03:47.388 --> 03:50.125
call. And if you're a truck driver being loaded,

03:50.125 --> 03:53.088
stay in your cab. Every operator does the Quarry

03:53.088 --> 03:55.500
Equipment Pre-Operational Inspection before the

03:55.500 --> 03:58.213
shift, and it's turned in at the scale house or

03:58.213 --> 03:59.188
on the app.

04:00.316 --> 04:03.166
On Level 1 there are overhead power lines.

04:03.166 --> 04:05.891
The rule is no dumping or parking near them,

04:05.891 --> 04:09.016
no raised beds and no tarping. At the plant,

04:09.016 --> 04:14.191
conveyors UC 1 through 4, C2, 30, 31 and 32 have

04:14.191 --> 04:17.254
pull cords or emergency stops, and so do the front

04:17.254 --> 04:19.941
fuel tank and the shop fuel tank. Learn where they

04:19.941 --> 04:21.353
are before you need one.

04:22.486 --> 04:25.936
Basic PPE is a hard hat, safety glasses,

04:25.936 --> 04:28.736
steel-toe boots, high-visibility clothing where

04:28.736 --> 04:31.874
required, and hearing protection as required.

04:31.874 --> 04:34.361
Hearing protection is required around the plant

04:34.361 --> 04:37.074
while it's running and around the mine fans.

04:37.074 --> 04:40.036
Respiratory protection is used when directed.

04:40.036 --> 04:42.511
If you're near a pond, sump or pump where you could

04:42.511 --> 04:45.599
fall into water, a life jacket is required.

04:45.599 --> 04:47.811
Eyewash bottles are at the scale house,

04:47.811 --> 04:50.424
the breakroom, the shop and the primary crusher

04:50.424 --> 04:53.861
MCC. The SDS binder is in the breakroom.

04:54.976 --> 04:58.189
In an underground emergency, stench gas is released

04:58.189 --> 05:01.176
into the intake fan, and warnings also come by

05:01.176 --> 05:04.501
radio and strobe lights. At the first sign of smoke,

05:04.501 --> 05:08.651
a CO alarm or stench gas, put on your W65 and get

05:08.651 --> 05:11.214
out by your escapeway. Before a blast,

05:11.214 --> 05:13.439
there's a siren and strobe beacons,

05:13.439 --> 05:15.826
and all entrances to the underground headers are

05:15.826 --> 05:18.826
blocked. Escapeways are marked on the mine maps

05:18.826 --> 05:22.376
with green arrows. Underground, the primary escapeway

05:22.376 --> 05:24.864
is marked with white reflectors on the ribs,

05:24.864 --> 05:27.139
and the secondary with blue reflectors,

05:27.139 --> 05:29.814
along with reflective signs and arrows.

05:29.814 --> 05:32.551
Escape maps are posted in the breakroom and on

05:32.551 --> 05:35.014
each level: in the shop on Level 1,

05:35.014 --> 05:37.814
at the primary crusher MCC on Level 2,

05:37.814 --> 05:41.014
and between the ramps at the porta john on Level 3.

05:41.014 --> 05:43.676
The gathering points are the tag board and a designated

05:43.676 --> 05:47.839
area behind the mine, outside the 22 North escapeway.

05:47.839 --> 05:50.951
On the CB, the scale house is channel 30 and the

05:50.951 --> 05:53.776
yard loaders are channel 19. Your instructor will

05:53.776 --> 05:56.564
walk you through the actual routes from your level.

05:56.564 --> 05:58.801
Mine rescue for all of our sites comes from the

05:58.801 --> 06:01.626
Kentucky Division of Mine Safety's Crestwood and

06:01.626 --> 06:03.688
Hazard mine rescue stations.

06:07.060 --> 06:10.735
From 2016 through mid-October 2026,

06:10.735 --> 06:15.085
MSHA records 21 reportable worker injuries at Boonesboro.

06:15.085 --> 06:17.935
Six were slips and falls, mostly missing a step

06:17.935 --> 06:20.223
climbing down haul trucks and loaders.

06:20.223 --> 06:22.823
Six came from handling materials like plates and

06:22.823 --> 06:25.673
drill steel. Three were powered haulage,

06:25.673 --> 06:28.435
three were hand tools, two were machinery,

06:28.435 --> 06:30.285
and one was face rock falling.

06:31.425 --> 06:34.375
Some of those cases teach a lesson worth remembering.

06:34.375 --> 06:37.575
In 2020, a scaler operator walked toward the face

06:37.575 --> 06:40.475
to pick up a lost tooth, and a rock fell onto his

06:40.475 --> 06:43.675
shoulder. Never walk up to a face to get a tool.

06:43.675 --> 06:47.362
In 2018, a worker's hand was on a tail pulley while

06:47.362 --> 06:50.575
someone else turned it. Lock out and block motion.

06:50.575 --> 06:53.812
In 2022, a miner riding on the front of a loader

06:53.812 --> 06:56.987
caught his leg. Ride only in a passenger seat.

06:56.987 --> 06:59.774
And three miners fell climbing down equipment.

06:59.774 --> 07:02.762
Face the machine and keep three points of contact.

07:03.878 --> 07:08.078
Inspectors issued 44 citations here from 2021 through

07:08.078 --> 07:12.153
mid-October 2026. The ones cited most were equipment

07:12.153 --> 07:14.828
defects not corrected, missing guards,

07:14.828 --> 07:17.828
insulating mats at switchgear, grounding tests,

07:17.828 --> 07:20.865
and conveyor emergency stops. The takeaway is that

07:20.865 --> 07:24.191
most Boonesboro injuries come from everyday tasks,

07:24.191 --> 07:27.541
not rare events. Pre-shift checks, guards,

07:27.541 --> 07:30.341
lockout and three points of contact prevent most

07:30.341 --> 07:31.740
of what's in this record.

07:32.877 --> 07:35.552
Before your first shift underground at Boonesboro,

07:35.552 --> 07:37.651
make sure you can answer four questions.

07:37.651 --> 07:40.164
Which level am I on today? What are my primary

07:40.164 --> 07:42.289
and secondary escapeways from there?

07:42.289 --> 07:44.651
Where is my gathering point? And who do I report

07:44.651 --> 07:47.364
to, and how do I reach them? If you can't answer

07:47.364 --> 07:49.614
all four, ask before you go in.

07:50.738 --> 07:53.901
Remember: your site's plans and procedures always

07:53.901 --> 07:55.401
override this video.
